### Filing rules (B274's, unchanged except where marked)
1. **Jira: HPSMPOC only, only these rows.** Copy B274's helpers from `.tools/b274/` (drafter `ls`: `jira.py read.py post.py search.py create.py create274.py rows_search274.py controls274.py mk_tickets274.py mk_comments274.py mk_c274.py mk_hist274.py apply274.py refscheck274.py namescan274.py cscan274.sh`) and `.tools/b198/lock.sh` into `.tools/b293/` and check each `cmp`-identical; adapt copies under new names (`create293.py` …); never edit the originals; **do not open anything else in `.tools/b274/` or any other seat's `.tools/b2*/` (its `texts/`, `logs/`, `_quarantine/`, the two `base-*.md` files are B274's records of its own run).** `JIRA_BASE_URL`, `JIRA_EMAIL` and `JIRA_API_TOKEN` are read BY NAME inside the process: never printed, never on argv, never in a file. Write verbs: create (7), comment (9), transition 41 (≤ 7), description edit (2, Part 1b).
2. **Search before EACH create.** JQL `project = HPSMPOC AND <clause>`, with the row's clauses verbatim, plus `labels = plan-b293-<rid>`, which must be 0. **Dedupe by SYMBOL and path, not phrasing.** Controls once per run: negative `text ~ "qjzxkwvp"` → 0 (drafter); ⚠ **not B274's `kxwzpqj` (B284 found 5 hits: B274's own tickets quote it)**; positive `text ~ "ce40ce07"` → 42 (drafter; 37 before B274's five tickets); `created >= "2026-10-19"` → 1 (HPSMPOC-293) before your first create; the highest key is HPSMPOC-293, so your first create should be **HPSMPOC-294**. **Your own tickets quote your control words in their "Duplicate search" line:** count the controls without this seat's new keys, and say so in each line. **A hit is EXISTING** when that ticket's subject or Done-when names the behaviour AND it is not met: comment on it instead of creating (counted; say which). A hit on a met or different Done-when is RELATED: create, and name it. A ticket this seat closes in Part 1 is RELATED (its Done-when is met). Record every JQL with its count, keys and status in STATUS, and quote it in the ticket's "Duplicate search" line.
3. **Shape (B274's; read HPSMPOC-291's description as the model).** Issue type `Task`. Summary `[<origin ids>] <title>`; **assert `len(Summary) ≤ 255` by program before the POST** (drafter's counts of the cells below: 243, 243, 242, 225, 242, 210, 237). If Jira still refuses one: do exactly what B265 FOUND 1 did (omit ONE span, put the brief's full Summary verbatim in the description's last paragraph) and say so. Description ADF, paragraphs in this order: `BLUF`; `Where` (`file:line @b3a7c27`; the drafter read every cite below at `b3a7c27`); `Severity` (the gate's); `Recommendation` (the gate's fix-shape, in prose); `Done when` (the gate's regression test; where the gate wrote none, the drafter's, labelled so); `Provenance` (`1_Project_Definition/Briefs/<STATUS>:<lines>`, related keys); `Duplicate search` (your JQL lines); `Filed by records seat B293 (Tuesday's brief 1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-10-19_B293_SEAT-R8_hpsmpoc-records-1019.md, Part 2 row <rid>), <run date by date +%F>`.
4. **Labels:** `b293-2026-10-19`, `plan-b293-<rid>`, the row's origin label (below; the four origin labels `b279-gate`, `b283-gate`, `b286-gate`, `b291-gate` hit 0 before you, as does `b293-2026-10-19`, which is expected), and existing topic labels only (drafter: `feedback` 14, `test` 25, `before-imports-on-hosted` 6; `imports` 0, so do not use it). **Assignee:** HPSMPOC-229's assignee `accountId` (drafter GET: `616503d4bfa2c1006b1971d1`, the same on -290, -291, -226); GET it, never write a display name.
